---
// About: who is asking and why, then how the numbers are worked out, then what has been read and
// what it moved. Made on 2026-10-21 from the Method and Story pages when the top bar was simplified
// (tracker pattern rule 4.21, ruled by John that day): the two pages' text is kept as it was, in
// components/AboutMethod.astro and components/AboutStory.astro, and /method/ and /story/ redirect to
// their parts here. The "Who is asking" section, which opened the method page, now opens this one.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AboutMethod from '../components/AboutMethod.astro';
import AboutStory from '../components/AboutStory.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About The Quiet Galaxy: who is asking, how the numbers are worked out, and what has moved them"
  description="Who built The Quiet Galaxy and why, how the number at the top of the site is computed from the seven pieces of the equation, and every paper read so far with whether it moved a range."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Who is asking, and how it works</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="section who" id="who">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Who is asking</p>
      <p>I'm John, and I write about AI, sentience and the spread of conscious life beyond Earth at <a href="https://sentient-horizons.com" rel="noopener">Sentient Horizons</a>. This is the sister of <a href="https://beltequation.com" rel="noopener">The Belt Equation</a>, where I track the odds of leaving Earth myself. Here the question is older and larger: whether anyone else is out there, and why we cannot tell. I wanted a place where the argument is laid out piece by piece, every number carries its source, and a new discovery moves the answer in public.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Why the name?</p>
      <p>Because that is the observed fact. The sky is quiet. Every explanation on this site is an answer to that one observation, and the site does not presume which answer is right: it works out, from the published numbers, how surprised we should be.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="about-layout">
    <nav class="about-side" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="about-side-h">On this page</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#who">Who is asking</a></li>
        <li>
          <a href="#method">How the numbers are worked out</a>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#the-multiplication">The multiplication</a></li>
            <li><a href="#why-a-spread">Why a spread, not a point</a></li>
            <li><a href="#how-a-value-is-picked">How a value is picked</a></li>
            <li><a href="#the-three-numbers">The three numbers</a></li>
            <li><a href="#where-the-ranges-come-from">Where the ranges come from</a></li>
            <li><a href="#what-moves-a-number">What moves a number</a></li>
            <li><a href="#what-the-explanations-are">What the explanations are</a></li>
            <li><a href="#what-is-not-in-the-method">What is not in the method</a></li>
            <li><a href="#the-working-documents">The working documents</a></li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#story">What has been read</a>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#find">Find a paper</a></li>
            <li><a href="#authors">Authors, A to Z</a></li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="about-side-foot"><a href="/reading/">This week's reading</a><br /><a href="/disagree/">Feedback</a></p>
    </nav>
    <div class="about-main">
      <AboutMethod />
      <AboutStory />
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The side navigation (added 2026-11-15, asked for by John that day): a list of the page's
     parts that stays in view beside the text on a wide screen, and sits above it on a narrow one. */
  .about-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 210px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 44px; align-items: start; }
  .about-main { min-width: 0; }
  .about-side { position: sticky; top: 84px; max-height: calc(100vh - 110px); overflow-y: auto; margin-top: 88px; padding: 2px 4px 2px 0; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.4; }
  .about-side-h { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .about-side ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .about-side > ul > li { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .about-side > ul > li > a { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .about-side ul ul { margin: 6px 0 0; padding-left: 12px; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .about-side ul ul li { margin: 0 0 5px; }
  .about-side a { color: var(--text-soft); text-decoration: none; }
  .about-side a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .about-side-foot { margin: 16px 0 0; padding-top: 12px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); line-height: 1.9; }
  :global(.about-main .about-part:first-child) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  :global(.about-main h2[id]) { scroll-margin-top: 84px; }
  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .about-layout { display: block; }
    .about-side { position: static; max-height: none; overflow: visible; margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 16px 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--panel); font-size: 15px; }
    .about-side ul ul li { margin: 0 0 8px; }
  }
  :global(.about-part) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 40px; padding-top: 48px; scroll-margin-top: 70px; }
  :global(.about-h) { font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 14px; }
</style>
